      "id": "Q7",
      "question": "What metabolic derangements require urgent correction beyond hyperkalemia?",
      "my_answer": "Metabolic acidosis (HCO3 14), hyperphosphatemia, hypocalcemia, and hyperuricemia.",
      "rationale": "Severe acidosis worsens hyperkalemia and myocardial function; may need continued bicarbonate. Hyperphosphatemia contributes to hypocalcemia and renal injury. Hypocalcemia (ionized not measured but likely) increases cardiac irritability. Hyperuricemia (from cell breakdown) can contribute to AKI through crystal nephropathy."
